<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- ADDED 17 Oct 2026 - the unfilled remainder of a countdown ring.

     android:useLevel is stated EXPLICITLY, and it is FALSE here - which is
     the opposite of what this file used to say, and the reason the ring had no
     visible track at all.

     WHAT THE PLATFORM DOES (GradientDrawable.java, buildRing):
         float sweep = st.mUseLevelForShape ? (360.0f * getLevel() / 10000.0f) : 360f;
     and mUseLevelForShape DEFAULTS TO TRUE (GradientState). So a ring shape
     with useLevel=true draws a sweep of 360 x level/10000 - and a level of
     zero draws NOTHING.

     ProgressBar.setVisualProgress sets the level on the layer with
     @android:id/progress and only on that layer (ProgressBar.java:1661-1685),
     so the TRACK keeps its own level, which is 0. With useLevel=true on the
     track, that means the track drew a zero-length sweep and was invisible:
     the Next Dose ring had no muted remainder, and the DoxyPEP card's
     "empty ring" - which the owner asked for by name on 20 Oct - had no ring
     on it at all. Both were visible on the device and neither was visible in
     the source.

     useLevel="false" makes the track ignore the level and always draw the
     full 360 degrees, which is what a track IS: the whole circle, with the
     arc drawn over the part that is left.

     The ARC keeps useLevel="true", because setProgressBar has to move its
     sweep - that is the whole point of the layer.

     Geometry: innerRadius 19dp + thickness 4dp = 23dp outer radius, so a 46dp
     view contains it exactly. Explicit dp rather than innerRadiusRatio/
     thicknessRatio because those ratios are fractions of whatever bounds the
     drawable is given, which the launcher rather than this app decides - and a
     ring drawn at 52dp inside a 46dp view is CLIPPED, not scaled.
     CHANGED 20 Oct 2026 from thickness 6dp to 4dp, which makes the hole
     38dp instead of 32dp. That is the room the ring's centre needs: the
     owner's instruction is that the COUNTDOWN goes in the ring and the fixed
     time goes below it, and the platform's countdown format ("6:18:35")
     measures 100px at 12sp on this device - it does not fit an 88px hole.

     MUST match widget_ring_arc.xml exactly - a mismatch draws two concentric
     rings of different diameters rather than one arc over one track. -->
<shape xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    android:shape="ring"
    android:innerRadius="19dp"
    android:thickness="4dp"
    android:useLevel="false">
    <solid android:color="@color/widget_ring_track" />
</shape>
